Z||000006||daved||12-01-2001||09:43 PM||||#1 must be related to your low battery voltage. Should be 14 Volts or more when running.  Could be:<BR>a. bad battery<BR>b. bad alternator<BR>c. High resistance connections.<P>For a. substitute a known good one is easiest<BR>for b. trying a. should tell you this<BR>and c. remove and clean all connections to battery and grounds.  Polish till metal shines, then lightly coat with vaseline.<BR>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
