Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||12-02-2001||02:12 AM||||#1.) Bad alternator or worn belt. Do the needles even move? If they do, they may not be getting enough juice to work espicially warm (engin takes more)<P>#2.) Water pump ready to retire.<P>#3.) see #1.<P>#4.) Bad fan switch, bad plug, dirty connections at switch, not getting hot enough (takes a long time at idle) or any of the afor mentioned items.||||reg||1
Z||000009||MR2KLR||12-02-2001||09:55 AM||||I was just out leting the car get hot I noticed that it starts to run crappy when the batt gets low. BUT the battery allways had enough juice to start the car. I have had a bad alt B4 and the car would stall out when the battery would die. How much does a new alt. cost for a 88? <P>I grounded the dark green wire like my haynes manual sad to test the temp switch nothing happend.<P>while the car was running I unpluged the coolant switch (in the water neck), The fan came on along with the check engine light the car also ran a bit better (less gurgleing at idle)<P>as for the water pump will it be OK for a while as long at I keep water in it. or do I NEED on right now?<P>Thanks<BR>Tom||||reg||1
